  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 111 PM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nOn Friday the upper level ridge centered across the Desert Southwest \nis forecast to strengthen. High temperatures on Friday will likely \nbe the hottest of the week. Highs will be in the upper 90s to near \n104 across the region. Overnight lows will be in the mid to upper 70s.\n\nFriday night into Saturday, the aforementioned upper level ridge \nwill begin to shift west. Meanwhile, a weak cold front will move \nsouth through the Plains and move into the Big Country early \nSaturday. This weak cold front will then track south across the area \non Saturday. There are low (20-30%) rain chances Friday night into \nSaturday associated with the cold front. Highs on Saturday will be \nslightly cooler, in the mid to upper 90s. Similar temperatures are \nforecast on Sunday with highs in the 90s. A slow warm up is then \nforecast into the first part of next week with highs in the mid 90s \nto near 100.",
